ey  has plunged into his memories of his  time serving in the navy where audiences  get a clear glimpse into the horrors the  youngest dutton experienced while  serving as his vision quest nears the  end the appearance of a young girl leads  casey to the top of a hill there he's  presented with two possible paths and is  told the girl will help him walk the one  he picks but he must decide the way his  wife monica later asks him what he's  seen casey tells her i saw the universe  it's an ominous revelation especially  because it's unclear what casey is  referring to it could be the duttons  whose ownership of the ranch is as  integral to their sense of identity as  their lives it could also refer to  casey's relationship with monica which  has been tested repeatedly throughout  the show casey's dreadfilled statement  has quickly become a source of much  speculation amongst yellowstone fans  several interpretations have been  suggested by fans who hang out on the  yellowstone subreddit as they debate  what casey's final line of season 4  ultimately means in the grand scheme of  the show's future redditors shared their  mixed opinions about what these eerie  words could mean one commenter wrote did  he mean the end of him and monica the  end of the human race the end of the  duttons or the ranch or the end of their  town or way of life they also added that  monica seemed to understand what casey  was getting at another redditor  suggested that the two pass represent  casey being forced to pick between his  relationship with monica and saving the  dutton-ranching empire whichever path he  chooses the other relationship will be  ended meanwhile another redditor wrote  that the divided path represents casey's  choice between the white world of the  duttons and the indigenous world of  monica and her family who were fighting  to get their land back from the duttons  whether or not any of these theories are  correct fans will have to wait for  season 5 of yellowstone to see what  happens  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  yellowstone are coming soon subscribe to  our youtube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you
 

